WEBVTT

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:06.100
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.930
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.010
Verse 14

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.010
The 
emotions 
experienced

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:14.360
If I could pick who I face in 
the Master match,

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:17.300
I'd want it to be Dr. Harada.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.960
<i>Suo...</i>

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:27.970
<i>Suo Hisashi...</i>

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:30.230
<i>The current Master...</i>

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:36.510
<i>If he defends his title one more time, 
he'll be an Eternal Master.</i>

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:46.360
<i>Slowly...</i>

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:49.090
<i>I can take this slowly.</i>

00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:50.880
<i>Just get up.</i>

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:51.790
<i>on a long September night, 
and then I saw a dawn moon</i>

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:54.460
<i>The great thing about karuta</i>

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:56.850
<i>is that there are no time limits.</i>

00:01:57.410 --> 00:01:59.270
<i>I can take it slowly.</i>

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:00.680
<i>Just get up.</i>

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:08.190
<b>Master and Queen Challenger Playoffs 
Sponsored by the National Karuta Association</b>

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:07.340
<i>I just kept playing with no strategy 
and no concern for my knee.</i>

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:10.350
<i>Was I dreaming or something?</i>

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:13.180
<i>I was sucked in.</i>

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:16.430
<i>I never expected to find a 17-year-old like him.</i>

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:19.200
<i>Sheesh...</i>

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:21.910
<b>Swoosh...</b>

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:21.920
<i>Sheesh.</i>

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:23.120
<b>Gulp</b>

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:25.860
It's getting cold.

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:28.250
<b>My bride...♥</b>

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:27.840
Use this.

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:35.150
<i>Sheesh.</i>

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:39.250
<i>Even when I'm not moving,
I can hear my knee throbbing.</i>

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:41.550
<i>Give me a break!</i>

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:44.350
<i>Too much outside noise could be fatal...</i>

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:46.060
<i>to my comeback!</i>

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:53.220
<i>The sky may hold the same moon</i>

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:53.770
<i>He gets to his opponent's right side that fast
when his play style isn't even that offensive?</i>

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:58.180
<i>A young man imitating a great predecessor...</i>

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:00.770
<i>I thought I could get away 
with seeing him that way.</i>

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:03.040
<i>But he's not.</i>

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:04.910
<i>He's the real deal.</i>

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:09.530
<i>No matter where the cards are moved to,
he's flexible and balanced enough to take them.</i>

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:12.930
<i>How can I beat him?</i>

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:15.850
<i>How?</i>

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:17.540
<i>Dr. Harada...</i>

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.850
<i>How can you put so much into this?</i>

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:24.120
"Put your entire youth into it 
without becoming stronger"?

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:26.810
Say that after you've actually done it.

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:30.590
<i>I've already put my youth into it.
 That's why it scares me.</i>

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:34.010
<i>What if there's nothing left at the end?</i>

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:37.290
<i>What if I end up with nothing but regrets?</i>

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:40.400
<i>Harada...</i>

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:43.890
<i>Thirty-one years ago,</i>

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:46.850
<i>when he challenged the Master 
for the first time,</i>

00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:49.460
<i>Harada was definitely strong.</i>

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:51.490
You almost had him, Harada-kun!

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:53.530
With a lucky break or two, 
you might've had a chance.

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:57.160
You probably didn't have time to practice, 
what with your med school residency.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:59.910
I'll take the Master title next time!

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:02.700
That kind of big talk suits you!

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:06.030
<i>No one doubted the momentum he had.</i>

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:09.550
<i>At age 26, he had the ultimate talent for karuta,</i>

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:11.840
<i>and his game sense was unmatched.</i>

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:13.680
<i>And yet...</i>

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:17.600
<i>His first posting as a doctor was in Okinawa.</i>

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:20.930
The ocean's blue, but there's 
no one to play karuta with!

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:23.480
<i>His next posting was in Hokkaido.</i>

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:26.250
All they have here are wooden cards!

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:29.950
<b>Harada Internal Medicine/Pediatrics</b>

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:29.960
<i>And by the time he finally opened 
his own practice in Tokyo...</i>

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:41.020
<i>he was 37 years old and no longer had 
his youthful hearing and reflexes.</i>

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:45.920
<i>His natural game sense had 
begun to grow clouded.</i>

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:50.370
<i>The tail feathers...</i>

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:50.640
<i>Dead card!</i>

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:57.080
<i>Said night was young when 
the false rooster's crow,</i>

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.090
<i>Another one!</i>

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:54.970
<i>Lunging like that on dead cards...</i>

00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:56.700
<i>Just like in the first round.</i>

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:59.100
<i>No, this was even stronger than that.</i>

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:03.460
<i>Thrusting at the opponent's lower right side 
in a way that can't be called a false start...</i>

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:04.610
<i>He's playing offense.</i>

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:08.110
<i>In the first round, I was extra careful</i>

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:10.150
<i>and put fewer cards on my right side.</i>

00:05:10.630 --> 00:05:14.630
<i>But Grandpa wouldn't do that.
He placed more emphasis on balance.</i>

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:17.110
<i>Besides all that...</i>

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:19.840
<i>the red that is the Tatsuta River</i>

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:19.840
<i>hence the name fall leaves</i>

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:19.840
<i>in my dreams, I creep closer to you</i>

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:19.390
<i>The cards remaining on my right side...</i>

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:21.130
<i>the red that is the Tatsuta River</i>

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:21.130
<i>hence the name fall leaves</i>

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:21.120
<i>I can take them.</i>

00:05:21.850 --> 00:05:22.810
<i>I will take them!</i>

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:27.580
<i>As the first frost...</i>

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:29.170
<i>H-He's being crazy again!</i>

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:31.910
<i>He launched his whole body toward 
his opponent's right side,</i>

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:33.440
<i>and only his arm reached for the left!</i>

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:35.620
<i>That'd make anyone fall over.</i>

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:37.430
<i>I got it, though!</i>

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:48.700
<i>as my concern this morning is 
as tangled as my black hair</i>

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:08.660
<i>May my sighs be blamed upon the moon,</i>

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:08.500
<i>Dr. Harada went for "May I see" 
but returned to "May my sighs"!</i>

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:10.340
<b>Again...!</b>

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:10.340
<i>And he kept blocking 
Wataya-kun the whole time!</i>

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:13.240
<i>I've never seen so much slamming 
and crashing in a match!</i>

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:16.000
<i>Are you a grade school kid?! 
What a disgrace!</i>

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:39.210
Thanks, Glasses.

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:44.640
<i>Not everyone is blessed with 
such abundant talent.</i>

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:49.520
Fine hairs inside the ear 
vibrate when air hits them.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:52.800
Continuous vibrating over time

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:55.880
wears down these fine hairs,
making it harder to hear higher pitches.

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:57.990
This is how ears age.

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:01.100
Once lost, the fine hairs in 
the ear never regenerate.

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:06.640
So I can never go back to being
a player with good game sense...

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:10.200
Dr. Harada! Dr. Harada!

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:12.350
Let's play karuta, Dr. Harada!

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:13.450
Yeah! Let's play!

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:16.530
Dr. Harada! I came in third 
at my school's tournament!

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:20.090
Hey, as a member of the Shiranami Society,
 you should've won, Yuta!

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:24.620
<i>Not everyone has good game sense.</i>

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:27.760
<i>I need to find a different weapon!</i>

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:37.550
Huh? Where are you going?

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:43.710
<i>The Shiranami Society teaches karuta that 
makes players with poor game sense stronger!</i>

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:50.530
<i>Impassioned vows exchanged over 
many a tear shed to last</i>

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:46.390
<i>Dead card!</i>

00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:48.260
<i>He attacked again, but did he stop himself?</i>

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:49.440
<i>Wait, did he?!</i>

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:53.350
Uh... You touched that, didn't you?

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:54.330
Nope.

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:56.500
B-But... I think you did...

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.080
<b>You touched
 "Impassionate"
 a little...</b>

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:59.090
If that's what you think, 
then send me a card.

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:02.540
<i>Nasty...</i>

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:13.170
<i>He lost one!</i>

00:08:13.490 --> 00:08:15.810
<i>Arata-kun lost a one-syllable 
card on his own side!</i>

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:24.940
<i>the sight of a midnight moon</i>

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:33.940
<i>He's putting the card he was sent 
on the right side for balance.</i>

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:37.190
<i>Even though he knows it'll be targeted...</i>

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:41.790
<i>This is what Grandpa would do, even if 
his right side was being targeted.</i>

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:44.190
<i>I'll fight for all the cards.</i>

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:46.960
<i>I'll take them wherever they are.</i>

00:08:47.770 --> 00:08:50.060
<i>Ten to six...</i>

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:52.460
<i>If there's any way to win from here, it's...</i>

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:57.880
<i>to attack without hesitation,
even if it breaks my personal style!</i>

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:00.480
<i>H-He got four in a row!</i>

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:02.350
Excuse me.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:04.350
Sorry.

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:08.480
Chihaya?

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:20.350
<i>The momentum isn't favoring me.</i>

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:22.740
<i>All the cards being read 
are on my right side.</i>

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:28.290
<i>the red that is the Tatsuta River</i>

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:28.290
<i>hence the name fall leaves</i>

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:27.300
<i>Should I abandon that side?</i>

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:31.900
<i>If I were still in grade school...</i>

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:33.750
<i>Arata, you're amazing!</i>

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:35.010
<i>You can totally do this!</i>

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:35.760
<i>Keep it up!</i>

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:40.210
<i>If I were still in middle school...</i>

00:09:40.210 --> 00:09:42.260
You're joining the track team?

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:45.510
You won't be able to play in 
most karuta tournaments, then.

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:48.030
Everything is for karuta.

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:51.020
I see. I'll be waiting for you anytime.

00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:57.660
<i>And in high school... I...</i>

00:09:58.890 --> 00:10:01.030
Stop concentrating on speed.

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:03.690
No matter how upset you are,

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:05.700
you must thank your opponent.

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:08.170
Feels like a team match, doesn't it?

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:13.060
<i>This year, I will be the challenger!</i>

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:16.780
<i>Dr. Harada...</i>

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:18.220
<i>You can do it!</i>

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:19.600
<i>Dr. Harada!</i>

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:21.430
<i>Dr. Harada!</i>

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:23.810
<i>You can do it!</i>

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:31.440
<i>Glasses...</i>

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:34.570
<i>I'm sure you have people on your side.</i>

00:10:34.970 --> 00:10:38.930
<i>You'll always have Master Wataya
standing beside you, too.</i>

00:10:39.220 --> 00:10:41.950
<i>But in the very end...</i>

00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:01.260
<i>No matter how many people are on your side,</i>

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:03.860
<i>no matter who taught you,</i>

00:11:03.860 --> 00:11:07.170
<i>in the very end...</i>

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:09.140
<i>when I cannot bear growing any 
weaker than I already have</i>

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:16.870
<i>It's a dead card!</i>

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:17.860
<i>A mistake!</i>

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:18.870
<i>Who hit it?</i>

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:20.370
<i>Who was it?!</i>

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:25.210
<i>Which one...</i>

00:11:25.210 --> 00:11:26.360
<i>...is the winner?!</i>

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:33.820
Thank you very much.

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:45.080
<i>Dr. Harada!</i>

00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:48.510
The winner of the Master challenger playoff is...

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:50.630
<i>It's Dr. Harada!</i>

00:11:50.630 --> 00:11:52.460
...Harada Hideo, grade 6!

00:12:08.980 --> 00:12:10.320
<i>He did it!</i>

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:13.040
<i>He did it!</i>

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:15.820
Coach Kitano? Where are you going?

00:12:15.820 --> 00:12:18.800
What difference does it 
make?! Don't follow me!

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:23.560
<i>In the very end, you're all alone...</i>

00:12:24.580 --> 00:12:25.800
<i>No.</i>

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:29.560
<i>In karuta, it's you and the reader.</i>

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:33.270
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:35.830
<i>Makino-san, your nasal tones...</i>

00:12:35.830 --> 00:12:38.560
Can't you stand up? What a sad sight.

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:42.560
<i>...resonated deeply within me.</i>

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:45.300
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:12:48.690 --> 00:12:50.210
Dr. Harada...

00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:52.330
You did it!

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:55.580
<b>Master and Queen Challenger Playoffs 
Sponsored by the National Karuta Association</b>

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:57.710
The awards ceremony will 
begin in ten minutes.

00:12:55.580 --> 00:13:01.090
<b>Master and Queen Challenger Playoffs 
Sponsored by the National Karuta Association</b>

00:12:57.710 --> 00:13:01.080
Would the four competitors please 
line up at the front once more?

00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:06.680
Hey.

00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:10.290
Did you have a scarf on before?

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:11.620
Where'd you get that?

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:13.420
Uh...

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:16.270
<b>Come to think of it...</b>

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:16.930
Master Suo lent it to me.

00:13:16.930 --> 00:13:17.700
Huh?!

00:13:18.070 --> 00:13:20.370
Don't get yourself indebted to the Master!

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:21.560
I'll take it back to him!

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:22.930
Th-Thanks...

00:13:33.390 --> 00:13:36.350
<i>In the end, I lunged at a 
dead card and faulted.</i>

00:13:37.700 --> 00:13:40.630
<i>Dr. Harada's hand went in 
the same direction...</i>

00:13:41.350 --> 00:13:43.390
<i>But he had the skill to dodge it.</i>

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:48.050
<i>the red that is the Tatsuta River
 hence the name fall leaves</i>

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:55.050
<i>"Gust" and "Impassionate"...</i>

00:13:55.050 --> 00:13:57.810
<i>I was determined to be 
the one to take those.</i>

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:03.280
<i>I never get that attached to 
specific cards, but today...</i>

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:06.610
<i>the red that is the Tatsuta River</i>

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:07.030
This one! I memorized this one today!

00:14:07.030 --> 00:14:09.760
And then there's the 
"chihaya furu" card!

00:14:09.760 --> 00:14:12.170
Wataya-kun said that the card 
has the same name as me!

00:14:13.050 --> 00:14:15.090
<i>I shouldn't have gotten fixated on those.</i>

00:14:15.990 --> 00:14:17.800
<i>Is that why I lost?</i>

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:20.330
<i>Grandpa...</i>

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:25.260
<i>No.</i>

00:14:26.740 --> 00:14:28.770
<i>I'm not Grandpa.</i>

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:31.850
<i>For me to win as myself...</i>

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:34.180
Arata...

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:37.150
Oh... Chihaya.

00:14:37.150 --> 00:14:39.010
Arata, um...

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:41.170
Th-That was close!

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:42.510
It was an incredible match!

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:46.020
Yeah...

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:50.780
You and Dr. Harada play in completely 
different ways. It was so interesting to see!

00:14:59.020 --> 00:15:01.950
What would you have done, Chihaya?

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:02.820
Huh?

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:04.760
At the end...

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:10.480
I play offensive karuta,

00:15:11.070 --> 00:15:13.180
so I think I would've sent both 
"Gust" and "Impassionate."

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:16.460
Because they're special.

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:25.920
The more I want a card, 
the faster I let it go.

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:30.120
Then I go in determined to take it.

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:48.800
I wouldn't want to talk to people who kept 
taking notes just so they could laugh at me.

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:50.710
Wataya-kun!

00:15:52.570 --> 00:15:53.810
Arata!

00:15:53.810 --> 00:15:56.010
Let's play karuta together forever!

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:08.400
I love you, Chihaya.

00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:28.290
Taichi might have told you this,

00:16:28.290 --> 00:16:31.410
but I'm planning to go to college here.

00:16:32.430 --> 00:16:34.170
If you want...

00:16:35.340 --> 00:16:37.420
let's play karuta together.

00:16:54.210 --> 00:16:59.140
What?!

00:17:02.970 --> 00:17:03.890
Suo—

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:07.160
I'm sorry!

00:17:07.930 --> 00:17:09.310
Thank you!

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:12.660
Suo-san...

00:17:13.140 --> 00:17:14.280
What?

00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:17.800
Thank you for lending this to her.

00:17:19.090 --> 00:17:20.240
Where is she?

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:21.050
I'm here in her place.

00:17:22.970 --> 00:17:26.070
And what are you to her?

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:31.340
"Put your entire youth into it 
without becoming stronger"?

00:17:32.140 --> 00:17:34.150
Say that after you've actually done it.

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:36.520
<i>Dr. Harada...</i>

00:17:37.520 --> 00:17:40.850
<i>Dr. Harada put in more than just his youth.</i>

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:43.310
I'm her boyfriend.

00:17:43.310 --> 00:17:44.820
Please don't try anything with her.

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:45.830
<b>Shock!</b>

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:48.210
<b>Divorce...</b>

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:47.120
<i>Divorce...</i>

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:56.020
Is it about time for the awards ceremony?

00:17:56.020 --> 00:17:59.220
Oh... Yes, it is... I think.

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:02.140
That was very manly of you.

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:17.150
<b>Master and Queen Challenger Playoffs 
Sponsored by the National Karuta Association</b>

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:25.890
Hey, where's Ayase?

00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:32.920
I don't think you fall short 
in either effort or talent,

00:18:34.310 --> 00:18:36.090
but did you figure out anything you lack?

00:18:37.410 --> 00:18:38.750
Meanness.

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:40.680
<b>What?!</b>

00:18:39.620 --> 00:18:40.670
Experience.

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:43.030
Passion.

00:18:43.730 --> 00:18:44.980
Love.

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:46.500
Love...

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:48.280
Love...

00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:52.360
Well, don't lose next time!

00:19:01.460 --> 00:19:04.490
Ayase! Where are you?!

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:14.920
Hello, Wakamiya residence.

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:15.540
<i>Hello—</i>

00:19:16.150 --> 00:19:16.850
<i>Hel—</i>

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:17.760
<i>He—</i>

00:19:19.910 --> 00:19:22.030
<i>What do you want, Suo-san?</i>

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:27.010
<i>If it's something worth hearing after
I hung up on you three times, I'll listen.</i>

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:32.260
Shinobu-chan, do you know who 
won the challenger playoffs?

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:34.520
Arata lost?

00:19:35.720 --> 00:19:36.640
Yeah.

00:19:38.230 --> 00:19:41.150
The veteran player won as 
the Queen challenger, too.

00:19:41.150 --> 00:19:44.760
<i>How? Was Arata feeling under the weather?</i>

00:19:44.760 --> 00:19:46.780
He didn't look that way to me.

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:52.540
It's like how a fresh apple loses 
in sweetness to a dried persimmon.

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:55.120
Huh? What does that mean?

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:57.550
<i>Be careful in the Queen match.</i>

00:19:57.550 --> 00:20:01.300
I think you're a fresh apple, too.

00:20:07.710 --> 00:20:09.670
Bye, Teach.

00:20:12.260 --> 00:20:13.870
What a dork!

00:20:18.040 --> 00:20:19.440
My bride...

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:22.970
That's the first time I've seen
Mr. Suo without his sunglasses on.

00:20:22.970 --> 00:20:24.190
Well, it is nighttime.

00:20:24.640 --> 00:20:28.710
I heard he's skipping the final prep camp
 the week before the center exam, too.

00:20:28.710 --> 00:20:31.460
I can't believe that guy! 
In more ways than one!

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:32.820
But his classes are easy to follow!

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:37.090
<i>I'll be in the Queen match next year.</i>

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:48.170
<i>Apples? Dried persimmons?</i>

00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:50.190
<i>Whatever.</i>

00:20:53.690 --> 00:21:05.820
<b>High School National Ogura Hundred Poets 
Karuta Championship</b>

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:56.890
<i>Even Wakamiya Shinobu isn't invincible.</i>

00:20:56.890 --> 00:21:00.470
<i>Wataya-kun grew up with proper instruction. 
He's a true thoroughbred.</i>

00:21:00.470 --> 00:21:03.600
<i>Maybe he's pulled ahead of 
Wakamiya-san, who plays alone.</i>

00:21:03.600 --> 00:21:05.740
<i>How long can she stay the Queen?</i>

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:10.510
<i>Be careful in the Queen match.</i>

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:19.700
Madam, the kimono maker is here.

00:21:22.960 --> 00:21:25.680
Shinobu! I told you not to 
play in the reception room!

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:27.000
You'll damage the tatami!

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:29.410
Also, that hairdo is really strange!

00:21:31.360 --> 00:21:35.060
<i>I think you're a fresh apple, too.</i>
